menu "TG28 SW test app"

    config TG28_SW_TEST_WITH_HARDWARE
        bool "Build the on-hardware TG28 tests instead of the pure logic tests"
        default n
        help
            When disabled (default) the test app builds test_tg28_sw.c, which
            exercises only the pure conversion logic and needs no PMIC. When
            enabled the app builds test_tg28_sw_hw.c, which talks to a real
            TG28 over I2C (SCL=GPIO33, SDA=GPIO34, IRQ=GPIO2, address 0x34)
            and requires a Candis-S31 board or a TG28 EVM.

endmenu
